      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #4, 2026-08-06): a node with
      ⍝ more than 8 members (attributes+children) forces
      ⍝ Value::get_new_member()/double_ravel() to grow the structured
      ⍝ value's member table. double_ravel() used to allocate the new
      ⍝ (doubled) ravel via `new Cell[]` and free the old one via
      ⍝ `delete []` (on a char*, so no destructor ran) -- mismatched with
      ⍝ init_ravel()/~Value(), which use std::allocator<Cell> throughout.
      ⍝ Confirmed via ASan alloc-dealloc-mismatch on this exact
      ⍝ expression before the fix. 11 children (+2 attributes) is enough
      ⍝ to force (at least) one growth.
      ⍝
      APL←⎕XML '<a><b x="1"/><c y="2"/><d/><e/><f/><g/><h/><i/><j/><k/><l/></a>'
      APL._1a._1b.⍙2x
1

      APL._1a._2c.⍙2y
2

      (14 "") ⎕XML APL._1a
⍙1

      (14 "_10k") ⎕XML APL._1a
_11l


      ⍝ Regression (Blake McBride, Bugs22 #7): ⎕XML accepted duplicate
      ⍝ attribute names in the same tag (XML 1.0 §3.1 WFC "Unique Att
      ⍝ Spec"), silently building two members for the same attribute.
      ⍝
      ⎕XML '<a b="1" b="2"/>'
DOMAIN ERROR+
      ⎕XML '<a b="1" b="2"/>'
      ^
      )SIC

      ⎕XML '<a b="1" c="2"/>'
._1a: □
._1a.⍙1:  ┌→┐
          │a│
          └─┘

._1a.⍙2b: ┌→┐
          │1│
          └─┘

._1a.⍙3c: ┌→┐
          │2│
          └─┘

      ⍝ Bugs28 #9 regression: a document nested past MAX_DEPTH left the
      ⍝ partially-built tree's XML_nodes (and their APL_values) leaked
      ⍝ -- Value::add_member() released the target Cell before
      ⍝ constructing its replacement PointerCell, which itself does the
      ⍝ depth check and can throw, leaving that Cell released but never
      ⍝ reconstructed. )CHECK then crashed walking the survivors: some
      ⍝ pointed at already-freed siblings, others at that half-dead Cell.
      ⍝
      ⍴⎕XML (780⍴'<a>'),1040⍴'</a>'
SYSTEM LIMIT (nesting depth)
      ⍴⎕XML(780⍴'<a>'),1040⍴'</a>'
       ^

      )SIC
      )CHECK BRIEF

